4.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img05.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img06.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img07.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img08.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img09.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img10.jpeg\",\"/uploads/images/en1-p2/page063_img11.jpeg\"]','Review all learned vocabulary from semester 2',9,NULL,2,NULL,'Review (Unit 18)',3),(92,NULL,NULL,'Greetings and introductions. Asking and giving names and ages. Identifying boys and girls.',2,NULL,'Ask and answer about names and ages. Introduce yourself and others. Review numbers 1-10.',1,NULL,1,NULL,'Hi, I\'m ... (Unit 1)',4),(93,NULL,NULL,'Food vocabulary: kunafeh, rice, meat, fish, chicken, salad, ice cream, chocolate. Talking about food likes. Numbers 11, 12, 13.',2,NULL,'Name common food items. Ask and answer \'What does he/she like?\'. Read numbers 11-13.',2,NULL,1,NULL,'In the kitchen (Unit 2)',4),(94,NULL,NULL,'Garden vocabulary: bee, butterfly, bird, flower, tree. Numbers 14, 15, 16. Talking about things in the garden using \'has\'.',2,NULL,'Name common garden creatures and plants. Use \'has\' in simple sentences. Read numbers 14-16.',3,NULL,1,NULL,'In the garden (Unit 3)',4),(95,NULL,NULL,'New body parts vocabulary: ear, eye, hair, shoulder. Using \'I/You/We have\' and \'He/She has\'. Simple commands. Numbers 17-20.',2,NULL,'Name new body parts. Use \'have\' and \'has\' correctly. Follow simple commands. Read numbers 17-20.',4,NULL,1,NULL,'My body (Unit 4)',4),(96,NULL,NULL,'Review: greetings, names, ages, food, garden vocabulary, body parts, numbers 1-20.',2,NULL,'Review the language and vocabulary from Units 1-4.',5,NULL,1,NULL,'Revision Units 1-4 (Unit 5)',4),(97,NULL,NULL,'Action commands: jump, hop, clap, open, close, come here, go there, be quiet. Negative commands using \'Don\'t\'.',2,NULL,'Understand and obey simple commands. Form negative commands with \'Don\'t\'.',6,NULL,1,NULL,'Jump! (Unit 6)',4),(98,NULL,NULL,'Living-room vocabulary: telephone, sofa, computer, rug, TV. Prepositions: on, in, under. Saying where things are.',2,NULL,'Name common living-room items. Use prepositions \'on/in/under\' correctly.',7,NULL,1,NULL,'My home (Unit 7)',4),(99,NULL,NULL,'Town places: mosque, church, shop, school, park, playground, house. Prepositions: next to, between. Saying where places are.',2,NULL,'Name places in town. Use \'next to\' and \'between\' to describe locations.',8,NULL,1,NULL,'My town (Unit 8)',4),(100,NULL,NULL,'Review: action commands, negative commands, living-room items, town places, prepositions.',2,NULL,'Review the language and vocabulary from Units 6-8.',9,NULL,1,NULL,'Revision Units 6-8 (Unit 9)',4),(101,NULL,NULL,'Hobbies vocabulary: playing football, dancing, swimming, drawing, reading, singing. Asking \'What do you like?\' and \'What does he/she like?\'.',2,NULL,'Name common hobbies. Ask and answer about likes using \'do\' and \'does\'.',1,NULL,2,NULL,'My hobbies (Unit 10)',4),(102,NULL,NULL,'Transport vocabulary: ship, plane, train, bus, van, car, bike. \'This\' and \'these\'. Adjectives: fast and slow, big and small.',2,NULL,'Name common forms of transport. Use \'this\' and \'these\'. Describe with fast/slow.',2,NULL,2,NULL,'Transport (Unit 11)',4),(103,NULL,NULL,'Classroom items: flag, pen, keyboard, mouse, ruler, eraser, crayon. Saying \'What can you see? I can see a flag.\' Using \'next to\'.',2,NULL,'Name common classroom items. Use \'can see\' and prepositions.',3,NULL,2,NULL,'Let\'s find out! (Unit 12)',4),(104,NULL,NULL,'Clothes vocabulary: sweater, socks, hat, pyjamas, boots, shirt. Saying \'I\'d like a new sweater\'. Describing clothes with colours.',2,NULL,'Name common clothes. Ask for items in a shop using \'I\'d like\'. Describe clothes with colours and size.',4,NULL,2,NULL,'Let\'s go shopping! (Unit 13)',4),(105,NULL,NULL,'Review: hobbies, transport, classroom items, clothes.',2,NULL,'Review the language and vocabulary from Units 10-13.',5,NULL,2,NULL,